---
import SeoArticle from "../../components/SeoArticle.astro";
import { faq } from "./faq";
---

<SeoArticle idPrefix="ws-seo" {faq}>
	<section aria-labelledby="ws-seo-how">
		<h2 id="ws-seo-how" class="sd-text-title">How to run a writing sprint</h2>
		<ol>
			<li>Choose a length: 10, 15 or 25 minutes, or your own, up to three hours.</li>
			<li>Press Start sprint and write. The timer counts down and the word count rises as you type.</li>
			<li>Pause if you are interrupted, or hide the timer if watching it makes you tense.</li>
			<li>When time is up, you see how many words you wrote and how long the sprint ran.</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="ws-seo-tips">
		<h2 id="ws-seo-tips" class="sd-text-title">Tips for a good sprint</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Decide what you will write before you press Start, even if it is only the next scene.</li>
			<li>Do not go back to fix things. Leave a note to yourself, such as [name?], and keep moving.</li>
			<li>Use the same length for a week and watch your word count. A steady number is easier to build on than a big one.</li>
			<li>Treat the draft as a first draft. The second draft is where you cut and reshape.</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section aria-labelledby="ws-seo-privacy">
		<h2 id="ws-seo-privacy" class="sd-text-title">Your draft stays in your browser</h2>
		<p>
			Nothing you write is sent to our servers. The draft is saved in your browser so it is waiting when you come back. There is no account and no limit on how many sprints you run.
		</p>
	</section>
</SeoArticle>
